From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:55:23 -0400
Subject: show the bare host in the steady state

Arc shows "example.com" where Chromium shows the whole URL, and docs/UI-SPEC.md
takes that as the target. LocationBarModelImpl already supports it through
LocationBarModelDelegate::ShouldTrimDisplayUrlAfterHostName, which iOS and the
picture-in-picture frame both turn on; desktop simply never overrode it.

The path is hidden only while the omnibox is unfocused. Focusing it restores
the full URL, and the two cases where the host alone cannot be trusted -- the
user has set kPreventUrlElisionsInOmnibox, or the certificate is bad -- keep
the whole URL visible.

Chrome ran a similar experiment and abandoned it over the risk that users judge
a page by a host that a long path could contradict. Ours is narrower, since the
full URL returns on focus, but it still deserves a user-facing setting before
1.0.

Why: the URL treatment is one of the four things that make the window read as
Arc rather than Chrome, and the extension point for it already exists upstream.
Removable when: a Stedding setting exists to control URL elision, at which point
this override reads the pref instead of deciding on its own.
---
 .../chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc       | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 .../chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.h        |  1 +
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc
index 4e23238dea745..e7fc8f4f28ca5 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc
@@ -89,6 +89,23 @@ bool ChromeLocationBarModelDelegate::ShouldPreventElision() {
   return net::IsCertStatusError(GetVisibleSecurityState()->cert_status);
 }
 
+bool ChromeLocationBarModelDelegate::ShouldTrimDisplayUrlAfterHostName() const {
+  // Stedding shows the bare host in the steady state, as Arc does; see
+  // docs/UI-SPEC.md. The full URL, including scheme and path, comes back the
+  // moment the omnibox takes focus.
+  //
+  // This repeats the body of `ShouldPreventElision()` rather than calling it,
+  // because that override is non-const. Keep the two in step: whenever the user
+  // has asked to always see the full URL, or the certificate is bad, the host
+  // alone is not enough to judge the page by and nothing may be trimmed.
+  Profile* const profile = GetProfile();
+  if (profile && profile->GetPrefs()->GetBoolean(
+                     omnibox::kPreventUrlElisionsInOmnibox)) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  return !net::IsCertStatusError(GetVisibleSecurityState()->cert_status);
+}
+
 bool ChromeLocationBarModelDelegate::ShouldDisplayURL() const {
   // Note: The order here is important.
   // - The WebUI test must come before the extension scheme test because there
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.h b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.h
index b4d971dbff35f..a8babc277ff17 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.h
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ class ChromeLocationBarModelDelegate : public LocationBarModelDelegate {
       const std::u16string& formatted_url) const override;
   bool GetURL(GURL* url) const override;
   bool ShouldPreventElision() override;
+  bool ShouldTrimDisplayUrlAfterHostName() const override;
   bool ShouldDisplayURL() const override;
   security_state::SecurityLevel GetSecurityLevel() const override;
   net::CertStatus GetCertStatus() const override;
